A reusable `ViewModifier` that lights up a translucent overlay while a drag of file URLs is over the target, and forwards dropped URLs to a callback.

## File

### `OneApps/VibeMachine/Views/Design/Workspace/Chat/Composer/Attachments/DropTargetOverlay.swift`

```swift
import SwiftUI
import UniformTypeIdentifiers

struct DropTargetOverlay: ViewModifier {
    let onDrop: ([URL]) -> Void
    @State private var isTargeted: Bool = false

    func body(content: Content) -> some View {
        content
            .overlay {
                if isTargeted {
                    ZStack {
                        Color.accentColor.opacity(0.15)
                        RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 12)
                            .strokeBorder(
                                Color.accentColor,
                                style: StrokeStyle(lineWidth: 2, dash: [6, 4])
                            )
                        Text("Drop to attach")
                            .font(.headline)
                    }
                    .allowsHitTesting(false)
                    .transition(.opacity)
                }
            }
            .onDrop(of: [.fileURL], isTargeted: $isTargeted) { providers in
                Task { @MainActor in
                    var urls: [URL] = []
                    for provider in providers {
                        if let url = try? await provider.loadItem(forTypeIdentifier: UTType.fileURL.identifier) as? URL {
                            urls.append(url)
                        } else if let data = try? await provider.loadItem(forTypeIdentifier: UTType.fileURL.identifier) as? Data,
                                  let url = URL(dataRepresentation: data, isAbsolute: true) {
                            urls.append(url)
                        }
                    }
                    if !urls.isEmpty { onDrop(urls) }
                }
                return true
            }
    }
}

extension View {
    func dropTargetOverlay(onDrop: @escaping ([URL]) -> Void) -> some View {
        modifier(DropTargetOverlay(onDrop: onDrop))
    }
}
```

The exact provider-decode incantation can vary; match what the rest of the codebase already does for `.fileURL` drops if there's a precedent. The contract is: dragging files over the modified view sets `isTargeted = true`, dropping invokes `onDrop` with the URLs and clears `isTargeted`.

## Application sites

- Apply to `ChatComposerView`'s shell. On drop, append one `.file(name: url.lastPathComponent, path: url.path, sizeString: "—")` per URL to the composer's `@State var attachments`.
- Document inline (a `// NOTE:` comment) that the modifier can also be applied to the whole `ChatPanelView` for whole-pane drop targeting; do NOT wire that here — it is an optional future extension.

The overlay must NOT block the underlying composer's hit testing while inactive (it only renders when `isTargeted`); when active it sets `.allowsHitTesting(false)` so the SwiftUI drop machinery still receives the drop event.

